  "output": "Here is the full performance analysis with actionable code examples:\n\n---\n\n## Performance Analysis\n\n### 1. N+1 Query Patterns (Backend)\n\n#### 1.1 Realtime Plugin — Sequential DB calls per mutation\n\n**`apps/api/src/server/plugins/realtime-plugin.ts`** — The `Message`, `Comment`, `Event`, and `GroupMember` handlers call the DB in a loop: each mutation triggers `conversationMemberIds()`, then `db.message.findUnique()`, then `db.conversation.update()` — 3+ round-trips per row.\n\n**Fix:** Batch the look-ups before the loop.\n\n```typescript\n// Before (inside a loop — O(n) queries):\nfor (const row of rows) {\n  const memberIds = await conversationMemberIds(row.conversationId)\n  const msg = await db.message.findUnique({ where: { id: row.id } })\n  await db.conversation.update({ ... })\n}\n\n// After — 3 queries total regardless of batch size:\nconst conversationIds = [...new Set(rows.map(r => r.conversationId))]\nconst [memberMap, messages] = await Promise.all([\n  db.conversationMember.findMany({\n    where: { conversationId: { in: conversationIds } },\n    select: { conversationId: true, userId: true },\n  }).then(ms => Map.groupBy(ms, m => m.conversationId)),\n  db.message.findMany({\n    where: { id: { in: rows.map(r => r.id) } },\n    include: { sender: true },\n  }),\n])\nfor (const row of rows) {\n  const memberIds = memberMap.get(row.conversationId)?.map(m => m.userId) ?? []\n  // ... emit events\n}\n```\n\n#### 1.2 Comment handler — 4-5 queries per comment\n\nEach comment fires `db.post.findUnique` + `mentionedReaders()` (which itself runs `db.group.findUnique` + `db.user.findMany`) + `db.comment.findUnique` for parent + `db.notification.findFirst` x2.\n\n**Fix:** Hoist all fetches to a single `Promise.all` before processing, and use `include` to avoid the follow-up look-ups:\n\n```typescript\nconst comment = await db.comment.findUnique({\n  where: { id: row.id },\n  include: { post: { include: { group: true } }, parent: true, author: true },\n})\n```\n\n---\n\n### 2. React Re-renders\n\n#### 2.1 `contacts-rail.tsx` — Sort on every render\n\n```tsx\n// apps/web/src/components/layout/contacts-rail.tsx:26-28\n// BAD — new array + sort on every render:\nconst sorted = [...people].sort(\n  (a, b) => Number(online.has(b.id)) - Number(online.has(a.id))\n)\n\n// GOOD — only recompute when inputs change:\nconst sorted = useMemo(\n  () => [...people].sort((a, b) => Number(online.has(b.id)) - Number(online.has(a.id))),\n  [people, online]\n)\n```\n\n#### 2.2 `conversation-list.tsx` — Filter/map on every render\n\n```tsx\n// apps/web/src/components/chat/conversation-list.tsx:50-66\n// GOOD:\nconst rows = useMemo(\n  () => (data ?? []).map(item => ({ item, title: conversationTitle(item.conversation, item.conversation.members, me.id) })),\n  [data, me.id]\n)\nconst filtered = useMemo(\n  () => term ? rows.filter(({ title }) => title.toLowerCase().includes(term.toLowerCase())) : rows,\n  [rows, term]\n)\n```\n\n#### 2.3 `message-list.tsx` — Status string rebuilt every render\n\n```tsx\n// apps/web/src/components/chat/message-list.tsx:148-164\n// GOOD — memoize the seen-by label:\nconst seenLabel = useMemo(() => {\n  const others = members.filter(m => m.userId !== me.id)\n  const seenBy = others.filter(m => m.lastReadAt >= last.createdAt)\n  return seenBy.length\n    ? `Seen by ${seenBy.map(m => m.user.name.split(/\\s+/)[0]).join(\", \")}`\n    : null\n}, [members, last.createdAt, me.id])\n```\n\n#### 2.4 Inline object in `MessageRow` props breaks memoization\n\n```tsx\n// apps/web/src/components/chat/message-list.tsx:236\n// BAD — new object reference every render:\n<MessageRow actions={{ ...actions, onJumpTo: jumpTo }} />\n\n// GOOD — stable reference:\nconst mergedActions = useMemo(() => ({ ...actions, onJumpTo: jumpTo }), [actions, jumpTo])\n<MessageRow actions={mergedActions} />\n```\n\n#### 2.5 `dayLabel` creates `new Date()` on every call inside message loop\n\n```tsx\n// apps/web/src/components/chat/message-list.tsx:39-48\n// BAD:\nd.getFullYear() === new Date().getFullYear()\n\n// GOOD — compute once outside the loop:\nconst thisYear = useNow().getFullYear() // useNow() is already available per AGENTS.md\nfunction dayLabel(d: Date, thisYear: number) { ... }\n```\n\n---\n\n### 3. Caching Opportunities\n\n#### 3.1 Realtime invalidation is too broad (highest impact)\n\n**`apps/web/src/hooks/use-realtime-sync.ts`** — `invalidateModels(qc, [\"comment\", \"post\"])` invalidates ALL post and comment queries across the app on every single comment change. This causes a full refetch storm.\n\n```typescript\n// apps/web/src/lib/query.ts — current:\nqueryClient.invalidateQueries({ queryKey: [model] })\n\n// GOOD — invalidate only the specific entity, not the whole model:\n// In use-realtime-sync.ts, emit the ID from the server event:\nuseSocketEvent(\"comment:changed\", ({ postId }) => {\n  qc.invalidateQueries({ queryKey: [\"comment\", { postId }] })\n  qc.invalidateQueries({ queryKey: [\"post\", { id: postId }] })\n})\n```\n\nThis requires the server event to include the parent ID — add it to `packages/shared/src/realtime-events.ts`.\n\n#### 3.2 Static data (org settings, user profiles) should have longer `staleTime`\n\n```typescript\n// In specific queries for rarely-changing data:\nconst { data: org } = useDbQuery(\n  [\"organization\", \"findUnique\", org.id],\n  () => db.organization.findUnique({ ... }),\n  { staleTime: 5 * 60_000 }  // 5 min instead of 30s\n)\n```\n\n#### 3.3 `conversationMemberIds` called once per socket event — cache it server-side\n\n```typescript\n// apps/api/src/server/plugins/realtime-plugin.ts\n// Simple in-process TTL cache avoids repeated DB hits for the same conversation:\nconst memberCache = new Map<string, { ids: string[]; exp: number }>()\nasync function conversationMemberIds(id: string) {\n  const cached = memberCache.get(id)\n  if (cached && cached.exp > Date.now()) return cached.ids\n  const rows = await db.conversationMember.findMany({ where: { conversationId: id }, select: { userId: true } })\n  const ids = rows.map(r => r.userId)\n  memberCache.set(id, { ids, exp: Date.now() + 30_000 })\n  return ids\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n### 4. Memory Leaks\n\n#### 4.1 `useSocketEvent` — listener accumulation on reconnect\n\n**`apps/web/src/hooks/use-socket.tsx`** — The effect depends on `[socket, event]`. If the `socket` reference changes on reconnect, a new listener is added. The issue is that the old `s.off(event, listener)` in the cleanup captures a potentially stale `listener` reference if `onEvent` prop changes.\n\n```tsx\n// GOOD — stable listener reference, separate effect for handler updates:\nuseEffect(() => {\n  if (!socket) return\n  const listener = (payload: any) => handlerRef.current(payload)\n  socket.on(event, listener)\n  return () => { socket.off(event, listener) }\n}, [socket, event]) // listener is stable — not re-created when handler changes\n\nconst handlerRef = useRef(onEvent)\nuseEffect(() => { handlerRef.current = onEvent }) // sync every render, no dep array\n```\n\n#### 4.2 Reminder worker — no batching of `notify()` calls\n\n**`apps/api/src/server/jobs/reminders.ts`** — `await notify(...)` is called inside a `for` loop for each due event. This is both slow (sequential) and risks partial failure leaving some events unnotified.\n\n```typescript\n// GOOD — parallel:\nawait Promise.all(due.map(event => notify([...attendeeIds], { ... })))\n```\n\n---\n\n### 5. Redundant Computations\n\n#### 5.1 `PresenceProvider` triggers full re-render tree on every presence update\n\n**`apps/web/src/hooks/use-presence.tsx`** — The context value is a `Set`. Every presence event creates a new `Set`, causing every `usePresence()` consumer (contacts rail, avatar badges, etc.) to re-render.\n\n**Fix:** Split into two contexts — one for the set of online IDs, and a selector-style hook:\n\n```tsx\n// Option 1 (quick win): memoize the context value to avoid reference churn\n// when the set contents haven't actually changed (already handled by the prev check)\n// The existing guard `if (prev.has(userId) === online) return prev` is correct — keep it.\n\n// Option 2 (better): expose a per-user hook to minimize subscriber scope:\nexport function useIsOnline(userId: string) {\n  return useContext(PresenceContext).has(userId)\n}\n// Components subscribe only to their user, not the full set.\n```\n\n---\n\n### Priority Order\n\n| Priority | Issue | File | Est. Impact |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Broad realtime invalidation | `use-realtime-sync.ts` | Eliminates 80%+ of unnecessary refetches |\n| 2 | N+1 in realtime plugin message/comment handlers | `realtime-plugin.ts` | Reduces DB load per message by 3-5x |\n| 3 | Presence provider cascade re-renders | `use-presence.tsx` | Reduces renders on every online/offline event |\n| 4 | Contacts rail sort + conversation list map/filter | `contacts-rail.tsx`, `conversation-list.tsx` | Prevents wasted work on every presence tick |\n| 5 | Server-side `conversationMemberIds` cache | `realtime-plugin.ts` | Eliminates repeat DB look-ups for hot conversations |\n| 6 | `useSocketEvent` listener leak on reconnect | `use-socket.tsx` | Prevents accumulating listeners over session lifetime |\n",
